  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Flame tongues, puff paths, ember drift, sweep width and the scorch's texture vary per cast. The 0.5 s inhale, the ignite time, the 0.2 s reach and the sweep speed stay fixed so the hit always lands at the same moment and a dodge window stays fair. The swath is laid across the line of fire (rotation 90) because it follows the sweep."
  },
  "director_notes": "Built from a request for a creature's fire breath, the kind a dragon uses; that is a genre, so nothing here copies a particular character's effect. Choices: (1) a 0.5 s inhale with a contracting ring, smoke wisps and a throbbing fire in the mouth gives the breath a clear wind-up and a fair dodge window; (2) the breath is a beam with style fire: a cone that widens to about 3x (spread) with a fBm temperature field ramping white-yellow core to orange to red, billowing flame puffs riding it so it has volume from every view, a white-hot jet inside that burns out along the cone, and embers shed off its edges floating up; (3) the far end sweeps across the target (sweep_px, one pass per 900 ms) and the ground marks follow the sweep: a glowing burn and ember cracks (add, short lifetime) over a long stretched scorch (alpha, outlives the spell). Impact uses additive smoke as flame billows, ember sparks flung outward and rising, and a dark smoke plume. Fire flickers slower than lightning (7-8 Hz). Sound: wind on the inhale, ignite plus a whoosh on release, a roaring fire for the stream and a quieter fire tail. The caster_hand anchor stands in for the creature's mouth; a game should attach it to the head bone. Heat haze is in the shader intent (distortion) only; the viewer does not draw it."
}
